WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.299
Despite the horrifying coronavirus numbers
I told you about earlier in the show, Donald

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:08.559
Trump is now holding daily rallies or even
multiple rallies each day.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:13.480
At least one of these rallies has now been
specifically tied to more than 20 cases of

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.150
corona virus.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.340
But that's a different story.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.800
The real story here for us today is that at
his latest rallies, Donald Trump has become

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.180
even more authoritarian than we've seen him
be before, including vowing to lock up the

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.840
Bidens, which we will also discuss in a moment.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:38.270
But these rallies are a true dystopian nightmare,
including Trump having the entire crowd boo

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.489
and jeer at the media.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:44.559
The exact opposite of a president who respects
a free press.

00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:51.159
But there's also a desperate and almost practical,
realistic element of Trump at these rallies.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:56.079
Trump seems to be recognizing that he indeed
might lose to Joe Biden in just a little over

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:57.210
two weeks.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:02.340
And Trump also seems to recognize or at least
admit that it would be very embarrassing for

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:08.670
him to lose because, as he says, Biden is
the worst candidate in history.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.010
That's not true.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.320
But the real reason it would be embarrassing
for Trump to lose is with all the bluster,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.940
with all the narcissism and the attacks on
the left and on Joe Biden, there would be

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:24.760
an irony in Trump losing to a guy he claims
is a terrible opponent.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:31.850
But there is one thing that Donald Trump has
now said in some form in terms of one state,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:36.860
like, for example, Trump has previously said
in the last couple of weeks, he goes to North

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.890
Carolina and says, North Carolina, if you
don't vote for me, I'm never coming back to

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:40.890
North Carolina.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.040
Iowa, if you don't vote for me, I'm never
coming back to Iowa.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.050
But now Trump has taken it up a notch, which
is actually quite interesting.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.740
Trump says if he loses to Joe Biden, he might
leave the country.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.280
Check out this clip from his Macon, Georgia,
rally a few days ago.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.890
I shouldn't jump because you know what?

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:04.370
Running against the worst candidate in the
history of presidential politics puts pressure

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.390
on me.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.060
Could you imagine if I lose my whole life?

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.060
What am I going to do?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.940
I'm going to say I lost to the worst candidate
in the history of politics.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.319
I'm not going to feel so good.

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:17.920
I have to leave the country.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.230
I don't know.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.500
So this is fascinating for a few reasons.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.109
First, it's clear Trump's primary feeling
will be embarrassment if he loses.

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:32.140
That's predictable, thanks to Trump's ego
and his narcissism.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.379
Now, there are some of you who will say narcissists
like Trump can't feel shame.

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:37.950
He will just say that it was rigged.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.889
Yes, of course he will say it.

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:44.810
But there is no doubt that privately at least,
it will be hugely embarrassing to Trump if

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.920
he loses to Joe Biden, which I would love
to see.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.760
Second, there's the idea of hiding.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.349
If he loses and this is becoming more and
more commonly mentioned indirectly, I've said

00:02:55.349 --> 00:03:02.650
before in the immediate aftermath, if Donald
Trump does lose, he may well deny he lost,

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:03.650
claim it was rigged.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.049
Be on Twitter 24/7, be doing but, you know,
press briefings all the time, accusing this,

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:10.689
that and the other person of cheating him
out of whatever.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:17.029
But if it is eventually undeniable that Trump
lost, if Joe Biden is going to be the next

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:21.180
president of the United States, I wouldn't
be shocked to see Trump all but disappear,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.050
just sort of evaporate into the ether.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:29.060
And the idea of never going to states he loses
again and now of leaving the country is another

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.060
indicator.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.060
Not literally.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.510
I don't believe Trump will literally leave
the country.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.430
But the underlying emotion of the idea is
there that Trump will just kind of disappear

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.299
and you won't hear from him again.

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:46.950
The reality is, I think the idea of a Trump
free United States would be so welcomed by

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:52.190
tens of millions at minimum, that the only
way Trump would really consider leaving the

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:58.459
United States leads us directly into layer
three of this conversation, which is the idea

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:03.249
of Donald Trump evading prosecution after
being president.

00:04:03.249 --> 00:04:04.590
Now, by the way.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:08.469
Is Trump says he's patriotic and his party
is patriotic.

00:04:08.469 --> 00:04:12.609
Is there anything patriotic about saying you
will abandon your country if your democratically

00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:13.609
removed?

00:04:13.609 --> 00:04:16.590
But again, I don't think it is literal.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:22.099
But think about what leaders leave their countries
after their reigns of terror are over.

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:27.340
It's authoritarian dictators fleeing arrest,
fleeing consequences.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:32.300
This is something we've come to see many times
globally when authoritarians lose their grip

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.539
on power.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:38.750
They go to a country without extradition to
live out the rest of their lives.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:44.090
And if I must tell you, there are plenty of
countries that would no doubt love to make

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:49.090
use of a former American president who will
just trash talk the United States.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.560
And Trump would easily find safe haven if
in plenty of places, if that's what he wanted

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:02.270
to do, he would become he would be welcomed
to become a sort of weaponized agent of social

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:05.150
discord, much like his presidency has been.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.150
I know many of you are obviously thinking
about Russia.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.259
This is bigger than Russia.

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:14.009
OK, now, the realization that I came to as
I was watching this farce take place in Macon,

00:05:14.009 --> 00:05:19.870
Georgia, was if we don't want all of this
exact same stuff to happen again in four years,

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.789
we have to make sure that this guy is removed.

00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:24.580
Now, all of these questions about Trump leaving
coming.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.010
All this different stuff, we've got to remove
him now.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.800
Talk about making America great again.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.159
By the way, Trump leaving and ideally taking
those kids of his with him.

00:05:34.159 --> 00:05:38.850
That would be one of the most powerful steps
Donald Trump could take to improve this country.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:42.860
And if you're not yet convinced of that, let's
look at some more clips from a recent rally

00:05:42.860 --> 00:07:30.219
that Donald Trump did.

